# Global rules #
################

# Build directories
build

# Compiled source
*.exe
*.o
*.d
*.class
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.lib
*.a
*.cof
*.hex
*.pyc
*.gch

# Python packaging build artefacts (pip install -e leaves egg-info)
*.egg-info/
*.egg
__pycache__/

# Packages
*.7z
*.bz2
*.dmg
*.gz
*.iso
*.jar
*.rar
*.tar
*.xz
*.zip

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.directory
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
*.swp

# Text editor backup files
*~

# Log files
*.log

# Blender cache
*.blend1

# OmniSim generated files
*.cache

# IDE files
.vscode

# Local rules #
###############

/msys64
# Shell launchers installed by src/omnisim/Makefile on Linux/macOS.
# bin/omnisim is the primary entry point, /webots the legacy alias -- both are
# copies of src/omnisim/launcher/omnisim-linux.sh (see bin/.gitignore for the
# omnisim-bin binary itself).
/bin/omnisim
/webots
/omnisim-controller
/webots.lnk
/omnisim_debug_output.txt
/util

# world thumbnail files
.*.jpg

# OmniSim runtime log (+ engine-written sidecars, e.g. omnisim_log.txt.newton.json)
/omnisim_log.txt*
/compile_commands.json
/tests/benchmarks/logs/
/tests/benchmarks/optim-logs/

# Temp launcher scripts
/launch_capture.bat
/launch_debug.bat

# Claude.ai
/.claude

# Large media files (>100MB GitHub limit) — host externally
/docs/media/videos/cuda_spheres_full.mp4

# Capture service output — local renders, never commit
/social/youtube_videos/captures/

# Social/marketing: never commit secrets or heavy video build outputs.
# (.env with live API keys lives OUTSIDE the repo at ~/.omnisim_social.env)
/social/.env
/social/**/.env
/social/x_videos/
# long-form campaign intermediates: per-shot trims, cards and the generated
# soundtrack that social/build_long_omnisim_campaign.py rebuilds from the
# tracked captures. Only the final reels under assets/ are tracked.
/social/public_launch/assets/_long_campaign/*
!/social/public_launch/assets/_long_campaign/.gitkeep

# Transient JSON dumps from headless runs / probes
/tmp_*.json

# RL: per-env temp world files written by OmniQuadEnv
projects/policies/worlds/.omniquad_rl_env*.wbt
projects/policies/worlds/.omniquad_rl_env*.omniworld
projects/policies/worlds/.omniquad_rl*_env*.wbt
projects/policies/worlds/.omniquad_rl*_env*.omniworld

# Harness scratch worlds written by scripts/harness/omnisim_harness.py
# (siblings of user worlds with a Supervisor robot appended)
**/.harness_*.wbt
**/.harness_*.omniworld

# Same idea for run-headless --fail-on-runaway (scripts/dev/headless_runner.py):
# a sibling world carrying the runaway_watchdog sampler, deleted at exit.
**/.omnisim_runaway_*.wbt
**/.omnisim_runaway_*.omniworld

# RL training run outputs
projects/policies/research/training/runs/

# In-engine trainer run outputs (checkpoints, state banks). Champion
# checkpoints are preserved by force-add at milestones (`git add -f`);
# already-tracked files stay tracked. Everything else here is a training
# by-product reproducible from the recipe + envs.
projects/policies/training/runs/

# RL exported policies — ignore untracked exports. The shipped deployable
# policies were force-added and stay tracked; new exports are ignored. The
# legacy omniquad policies that used to be whitelisted here were archived to
# projects/policies/research/policies/ on 2026-06-26 (see below).
projects/policies/research/inference/policies/*/

# Archived non-working RL experiments (moved to projects/policies/research/ 2026-06-26).
# The tracked source (controllers/worlds/runners + the canonical legacy policies
# and the ghost v6) is committed; ignore the bulky untracked policy blobs and the
# untracked ghost-policy exploration versions that came along for the ride.
projects/policies/research/policies/*/
projects/policies/research/controllers/g1_ghost_walk/g1_ghost_walk*.onnx
projects/policies/research/controllers/g1_ghost_walk/g1_ghost_walk*.onnx.data
projects/policies/research/controllers/g1_ghost_walk/g1_ghost_walk*.pt

# RL: current_command.txt is written per-eval and not committed
projects/policies/research/inference/current_command.txt

# MJX URDF preprocessing cache, regenerated by _urdf_to_mjcf.load_or_convert()
# on every training run. The rule keeps NEW generated copies out of git; the
# 11 tracked *.mjcf.xml under projects/robots/unitree/*/urdf/ were force-added
# (`git add -f`) and stay tracked -- they carry no absolute or host paths.
*.rewritten.urdf
*.mjcf.xml

.tmp/

# pytest-benchmark output dir, written wherever pytest is invoked from.
.benchmarks/

# Windows GPU driver crash dir — driver writes here when run from this cwd
/NVIDIA Corporation/

# warp's kernel cache — Newton/warp writes NVIDIA/warp/Cache/<version>/ into the
# process cwd, which for an engine run is the repo root. Regenerable (warp
# rebuilds what it needs) and tens of MB, so it must never reach `git status`.
/NVIDIA/

# Runtime artifacts at repo root — written by launch.bat, demo runs,
# headless harnesses, and capture sessions. These should never be
# committed; they pile up in `git status` and confuse new contributors.
/fps_sweep.summary.txt
/_tmp_*
/MUJOCO_LOG.TXT

# Capture-time scratch worlds (leading dot prefix).
distribution/generated_worlds/.capture_*.wbt

# Heavy regenerable Mars variants (8-31 MB each) untracked 2026-06-27: not
# referenced by demos.json or any runtime loader, deterministically
# regenerable via `omniworld generate mars` from the kept .seed.json sidecars.
# Untracked to stop multi-MB packfile churn; the demo `mars.wbt` stays tracked.
distribution/generated_worlds/mars_big.wbt
distribution/generated_worlds/mars_max.wbt
distribution/generated_worlds/mars_small.wbt

# Dev-time scratch (construction-site env iteration, duel diagnostic
# outputs, one-off Python analysis scripts, ad-hoc PNGs).
projects/_scratch/
/_scratch/

# Agent/tool session scratch (`outputs/<session-uuid>/`), including a symlinked
# node_modules. Local run output, never source -- and it can hold working data
# that must not enter git history.
/outputs/

# OmniSim per-world perspective files (viewpoint position, dock layout,
# scene-tree expansion state) written next to a world when it is saved in
# the GUI. These rules keep NEW per-user copies out of git -- every GUI save
# rewrites the file, so an unignored one would churn on every clone. They
# are NOT "generated, not source": the engine reads them back as the
# world's authored opening viewpoint (src/omnisim/core/OmPerspectiveFileFormat.hpp,
# src/omnisim/gui/OmView3D.cpp), and 73 tracked `.<world>.wbproj` files
# (2026-09-02: 65 under projects/samples, the rest in projects/robots,
# projects/languages, tests/ and scripts/)
# ARE the shipped samples' viewpoints. They were force-added, stay tracked,
# and an ignore rule never untracks an already-tracked path -- `git add -f`
# a new one when a sample's viewpoint is meant to ship. DUAL-READ /
# SINGLE-WRITE: `.wbproj` is the legacy name, still read forever;
# `.omniperspective` is the only one written now.
.*.wbproj
.*.omniperspective
# Foundry's camera lock is authored gameplay behavior: WASD controls the robot.
!projects/robot_combat/orc/worlds/.orc_foundry.omniperspective

# Machine-generated training data (PGM crops collected from sim runs,
# consumed by scripts/dev/train_anypick_classifier.py). Regenerable, never committed.
projects/policies/research/training/datasets/
# Pick-and-place demo controllers write per-run result dumps next to the
# controller (anypick / bin-picking experiments). Un-anchored so they match
# in the controller subdirs too, not just the repo root.
_anypick_*.txt
_binpick_*.txt
_universal_*.txt
_cell_*.txt
# Same class, JSON: the OMNIARM6 2F-140 pick-and-place controller writes its
# per-run verdict next to itself (PICK_OUT, omniarm6_2f140_pick_place.py).
_2f140_pick_result.json
# AgentBench R1 lane controllers write per-run telemetry next to their .py.
# Regenerable by rerunning the probe, and a stale copy contradicts the lane's
# committed verdict -- so it must never be the thing anyone reads.
tests/benchmarks/agentbench/**/controllers/*/drive_probe.json
tests/benchmarks/agentbench/**/controllers/*/r1_oracle_telemetry.json
# AgentBench BuildScale run workspaces at the repo root, one per (sim, level,
# arm) attempt: a copied clean_project/, the replay run, and the raw engine
# logs. A full campaign leaves dozens and they reached 142 MB before this rule
# existed. The DERIVED facts are what a claim rests on and those are committed
# under preregister/v1/build_scale_gate_records/evidence/ -- these dirs are the
# raw substrate behind them. Regenerable by rerunning the level.
# ⚠ Before deleting one, check it is not named in a committed facts.json: eight
# of them back the published 2026-08-13 gate records, and the level-250 pair
# holds a complete 9/9 PASS that has no gate record yet.
.agentbench-*/
.agentbench-*.pid
# Machine-local run residue, consolidated out of the repo root (2026-08-15).
# The root had accumulated 39 loose entries: 20 .agentbench-buildscale-* run
# workspaces plus ~19 one-off engine/probe logs. They now live under
#   .local-runs/agentbench/   the BuildScale workspaces described above --
#                             including the eight that back the published
#                             2026-08-13 gate records, so the ⚠ above still
#                             applies, just one directory deeper
#   .local-runs/logs/         husky/omniquad/swarm probe logs, fps_sweep summary,
#                             MUJOCO_LOG.TXT, a grep stackdump
# Nothing resolves these paths: the .agentbench-* strings inside the committed
# facts.json files are PROVENANCE (log_path / world), not dependencies -- the
# gate resolves only source_sha256 and run_evidence_sha256, and zero of those
# keys name a root run dir. Verified before the move.
# NOT moved: omnisim_log.txt and its sidecars, which the engine writes live.
.local-runs/
# Worlds authored by a comparison-lane agent during an AgentBench/ladder run.
# The lane preserves its own workspace under results/; a copy left behind in a
# demo directory is residue, and it is not held to docs/WORLD_RECIPE.md.
_codex_*.wbt
_codex_*.omniworld
# Controller _dbg() trace scaffolding (e.g. g1_seated_mimic). Regenerable.
*.dbg

# Raw CAD source drops (STEP/STP/IGES assemblies).
# These are large input artifacts; the colour-correct meshes produced by
# scripts/dev/step_to_urdf.py under projects/robots/.../meshes/ are the
# committed, reproducible deliverable. Keep the originals here, untracked.
/3d-models/
# same thing with the other separator -- the 2F-140 CAD landed in 3d_models/,
# and a 20 MB .STEP in git history is exactly what docs/developer/step-to-urdf.md
# says not to do (the tessellated meshes are the reproducible deliverable).
/3d_models/

# Install-conformance report bundles (python -m omnisim verify-install --report).
# Per-machine self-test output; regenerable, scrub-by-default, never committed.
/install-reports/

# Per-run agent usage telemetry written by `omnisim run-agent` at runtime
# (omnilink-reports/usage/<agent>/<timestamp>.json). Regenerable runtime output;
# keep the usage/README.md tracked but never commit the per-run snapshots.
/omnilink-reports/usage/*/*.json

# in-engine RL training outputs (reproducible)
projects/policies/research/rl_inengine/runs/

# stray scratch capture
_scratch_paper_text.txt

# Proprietary core fonts (Microsoft/Monotype) — cannot be redistributed under
# Apache-2.0. OmniSim ships metric-compatible Liberation/DejaVu replacements and
# maps the legacy names onto them (see WbStandardPaths::shippedFontFile).
resources/fonts/Arial*.ttf
resources/fonts/Times New Roman*.ttf
resources/fonts/Tahoma*.ttf
resources/fonts/Verdana*.ttf
resources/fonts/Palatino*.ttf
resources/fonts/Lucida*.ttf
resources/fonts/Trebuchet*.ttf
resources/fonts/Georgia*.ttf
resources/fonts/Courier New*.ttf

# tests/command_test.py writes its fixture slave into the CURRENT directory,
# so running the suite from the repo root drops it here. tests/.gitignore's
# /slave.py only covers tests/ -- without this it shows up untracked at the
# root and a broad `git add` would publish it.
/slave.py
# Git Bash crash dumps.
*.stackdump

# Vendor material supplied for integration work, NOT ours to redistribute:
# third-party SDKs, API manuals and client modules dropped here for reference.
# This tree is Apache-2.0 and targets a public snapshot, and this directory
# once sat UNTRACKED-but-not-ignored, so a single `git add -A` would have
# committed a proprietary SDK and its manual into it. Read such material in
# place; never vendor it.
/external_docs/

# Per-controller run output (telemetry JSONL, pad traces). Written by demo
# controllers at runtime; never evidence -- committed numbers live in world
# headers and tests/benchmarks/. See v7.0.0 CHANGELOG.
.build_tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local run residue (added 2026-08-24, pre-v8 audit).
#
# Each pattern below is here because it ALREADY produced tracked debris or an
# unignored file at the repo root. `_*_result.txt` is the one that actually bit:
# two controller result dumps were committed and shipped in v7.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*_result.txt
*.orig
*.rej
*.bak

# Harness / probe / A-B scratch worlds written next to the world they probe.
# The `.capture_*` rule previously existed only under distribution/generated_worlds/,
# which is why projects/omni_quest/worlds/.capture_*.omniworld slipped through.
**/.capture_*.omniworld
**/.ab_*.omniworld
**/.ao_probe_*.omniworld
**/.scratch_*.omniworld
**/_scratch_*/

# Open-loop diff-drive stall-torque probe rig (2026-09-11): sibling copies of
# three chat worlds with probe_diffdrive in place of the bridge, controllerArgs
# pointing at a session scratchpad. They are the measurement behind the wheel
# armature change in omnisim_newton_runtime.py; drop these two lines if the
# probe ships with that change.
/projects/samples/demos/worlds/chat/probe_*.omniworld
/projects/samples/demos/controllers/probe_diffdrive/

# The Franka Panda was archived 2026-09-02 (docs/ARCHIVE.md; git show
# f79b19a70:projects/robots/franka_emika/panda/...) and restored locally on
# 2026-09-11 for an outreach evaluation. Whether to un-archive it properly is
# an open decision; until it is taken the 11 MB restore stays a local file.
# Un-archiving means deleting this rule, a world that names the robot, a
# PROVENANCE.md, and removing its rows from docs/ARCHIVE.md.
/projects/robots/franka_emika/panda/

# Local scaffolding directory at the repo root (fleet_cam.py writes fleet_frames/ into it).
/youtube_videos/

# Local release/verification scratch (added 2026-08-26, omnisim-mcp packaging).
#
# Each is a throwaway working area produced while preparing a release, and each
# was untracked-but-unignored at the repo root, i.e. one `git add -A` away from
# being committed. `.local-release-tools/` is a 65 MB build/publish virtualenv,
# `.local-wheel-check/` is a clean-install target used to prove the built wheel
# imports, and `.public-release-worktree/` is a git worktree of the public
# snapshot -- a whole second checkout that must never nest inside this one.
/.local-release-tools/
/.local-wheel-check/
/.public-release-worktree/

# Python build artifacts for the packaged sidecars. The wheel and sdist are
# rebuilt by `python -m build` and published from CI (Trusted Publishing), so a
# committed copy is stale the moment the source changes.
packages/*/dist/

# Session scratch at the repo root (downloaded PDFs, review contact sheets) -- never repo content.
/tmp/

# Coding-agent scratch workspaces at the repo root (Codex sessions). Working
# material only -- anything worth keeping gets moved into a real repo path.
# `/.tmp-*/` covers every per-session dir (governed-swarm-review, localappdata,
# outreach-candidates, warp-cache, uv-cache-*, ...); `/.tmp_*` the loose files.
/.codex-tmp/
/.tmp-*/
/.tmp_*

# Outreach-pilot workspaces (social/launch/pilots/*): local virtualenvs,
# tool caches, build products, and clones of the recipient's own repos
# (name-<hash> checkouts). The pilot's evidence (README, traces, results,
# scripts) is tracked; the third-party source and rebuildables are not.
/social/launch/pilots/**/.venv/
/social/launch/pilots/**/.pytest-cache/
/social/launch/pilots/**/.pytest-tmp/
/social/launch/pilots/**/build/
/social/launch/pilots/**/upstream-*/
/social/launch/pilots/**/firmware-[0-9a-f]*/
/social/launch/pilots/**/hardware-[0-9a-f]*/
/social/launch/pilots/**/robot-[0-9a-f]*/
/social/launch/pilots/**/simulation-[0-9a-f]*/
/social/launch/pilots/luis_nav2/fork/
/social/launch/pilots/orion/.controller-python-shim/
# PPO pilot: keep each seed's best checkpoint (the eval input); the periodic
# intermediate checkpoints and tensorboard logs are training residue.
/social/launch/pilots/ppo_robot_controller/results/training/**/model_update*.pt
/social/launch/pilots/ppo_robot_controller/results/training/**/logs/

# Reply-wave workspaces (social/launch/pilots/replies_*): each recipient's
# own repo is cloned as a sibling of our evaluation. Our evaluation worlds,
# controllers, and reports are tracked; the third-party clones are not.
#
# 2026-09-12: this used to read `/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/` with a
# single exception for `evaluations/`. Early waves nested our work under
# `replies_<date>/evaluations/<name>/`, so the exception covered it. The two
# newest waves put our work directly at `replies_<date>/<name>/` instead, and
# the rule silently stopped protecting it: 70 evaluations and 5,478 files --
# the whole 2026-09-12 wave, including a full CPG gait-transition report --
# were untracked and one `git clean` from gone.
#
# The fix ignores wave contents by DEFAULT and re-includes the artifacts we
# author, rather than depending on where a wave happens to put them. Bulk run
# output stays out: 450 MB of logs/stdio/screenshots and 267 MB of raw trace
# CSV/JSON per wave, against 3.8 MB of worlds, controllers and reports.
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**
# Descend into directories, otherwise the re-includes below can never match.
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/
# What we author, and want back after any checkout.
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.md
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.py
# 2026-09-22: C++ too. The excitation-supervised port's adapter is a header
# and two programs that LINK a correspondent's library, and they are the rig
# behind a parity result already emailed to him -- a gitignored rig cannot
# re-certify a figure we have already sent. Safe to re-include now only
# because the `*_src/` rules below keep correspondents' own clones out.
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.cpp
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.hpp
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.h
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.omniworld
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.wbt
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.urdf
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.wrl
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/**/*.proto
# Third-party material re-excluded: a correspondent's own repo, and the robot
# description packages we clone to import from. Not ours to vendor.
#
# 2026-09-15: `repo/` and `fork/` are the names we USUALLY give a clone, not the
# names every wave gave one. `replies_2026_09_12/ur5_pondinesh/ur5_repo/` is a
# 55 MB nested checkout of the recipient's Pybullet_UR5_RRT (12 MB of it .git),
# and the `*.py` / `*.md` re-includes above pulled its sources back in. The
# suffix form covers `<anything>_repo/` without touching a tracked path -- there
# are none.
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/repo/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/*_repo/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/fork/
#
# 2026-09-22: the same bug again, twice over. This wave cloned three
# correspondents' repositories as `yash_src/`, `cbfjax_src/` and `ken_src/`,
# and put them at the WAVE ROOT rather than inside a per-thread directory. So
# neither the suffix (`_src`, not `_repo`) nor the depth (`replies_*/<clone>/`,
# not `replies_*/<thread>/<clone>/`) matched anything above, and the `*.py` /
# `*.md` re-includes pulled a correspondent's own sources back in -- including
# a nested .git, which commits as an unresolvable gitlink.
# Cover the `_src` suffix at both depths, and the clone-at-wave-root shape for
# the suffixes already named.
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*_src/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/*_src/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/repo/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*_repo/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/fork/

# Company-pilot workspaces (social/launch/pilots/companies/*). The rig we
# author is TRACKED -- probe scripts, generated worlds, evidence dumps,
# RESULT.md, DRAFT_EMAIL -- because a gitignored rig cannot re-certify a
# figure we already emailed. What stays out is the recipient's own source,
# cloned in beside the rig to import from: `repo/`, `repos/`, `upstream/` and
# linorobot's `hardware/`. Four of those are nested git checkouts, which would
# otherwise commit as an unresolvable gitlink rather than as files.
#
# Named directory by directory rather than ignoring the workspace by default
# and re-including our file types -- see the replies_* note above for what the
# default-ignore shape cost us on 2026-09-12.
/social/launch/pilots/companies/*/repo/
/social/launch/pilots/companies/*/repos/
/social/launch/pilots/companies/*/upstream/
/social/launch/pilots/companies/*/hardware/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/external_now/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/*/merged_copy/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/external/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/*_description/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/meshes/
# Interpreter and dependency trees. The `!.../**/` line above re-includes every
# directory, which overrides earlier rules, so these must be restated here --
# one .venv/Lib alone carries 4,767 .py files.
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/.venv/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/.deps/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/deps_*/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/site-packages/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/node_modules/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/__pycache__/
# Engine run residue: regenerable, and the reports quote what matters.
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/logs/
#
# Waves that used the `evaluations/` layout: everything BESIDE `evaluations/`
# at that level is the correspondent's own cloned repo, which is what the
# original rule was protecting against. Listed per wave rather than as a
# pattern because the layout is a property of each wave, not of the tree, and
# the two newest waves (2026-09-03, 2026-09-12) deliberately do not use it --
# there, the direct children ARE our evaluations and stay tracked.
/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_08_31/*/
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_08_31/evaluations/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_01/*/
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_01/evaluations/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_02/*/
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_02/evaluations/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_07/*/
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_07/evaluations/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_08/*/
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_08/evaluations/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_09/*/
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_09/evaluations/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_10/*/
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_10/evaluations/
/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_11/*/
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_2026_09_11/evaluations/

# Warp JIT kernel caches left next to pilot evaluation runs.
/social/launch/pilots/**/warp_cache_*/
/social/launch/pilots/**/warp_cache/
/social/launch/pilots/**/*_warp_cache/

# Participants' CAD sources and the meshes step_to_urdf derives from them:
# third-party geometry, rebuildable from the source_repository / source_commit
# the evaluation's review JSON records. The URDF, omnisim.yaml and worlds we
# generated from them stay tracked.
/social/launch/pilots/**/*.step
/social/launch/pilots/**/*.stp
/social/launch/pilots/**/meshes/

# base64 transport copies of attachment zips (the zip itself is *.zip above).
/social/launch/pilots/**/*.b64

# omnitug500_mcl_record writes its seeded MCL dataset (poses, 512-beam scans,
# meta) next to the controller; a run regenerates it byte-for-byte.
/projects/robots/omnisim/omnitug500/controllers/omnitug500_mcl_record/out/

# Bounded reply-wave evaluation workspaces (social/launch/evaluations/<date>/):
# the local virtualenv, pytest/zig caches and participants' upstream clones are
# never sources -- same treatment as the pilots' equivalents above.
/social/launch/evaluations/**/.venv/
/social/launch/evaluations/**/tmp/
/social/launch/evaluations/**/repos/
# A vendored Python stack (scipy et al.) an evaluation copied next to its trace.
/social/launch/evaluations/**/vendor/
# Participants' derived meshes and a participant project's debug symbols left
# beside its evaluation: third-party geometry and build products, rebuildable
# from the source_repository / source_commit the review JSON records.
/social/launch/evaluations/**/*.stl
/social/launch/evaluations/**/*.pdb
# pnpm's content-addressable store, left at the repo root by one of those evaluations.
/.pnpm-store/

# Hidden sibling copies of a world (.sweep_*.omniworld, .before_*.omniworld,
# .<name>_shifted.omniworld ...): the scratch a run script writes next to the
# world it varies (a copy must be a sibling for its relative URLs to resolve).
# tests/physics/worlds/.h2diag.omniworld predates this rule and stays tracked.
.*.omniworld

# ...but a reply-wave evaluation's own worlds are EVIDENCE, not scratch. The
# rule above is a blanket and git is last-match-wins, so it silently re-ignored
# 102 worlds inside replies_2026_09_12/ that the re-includes in the reply-wave
# block had just recovered -- the scenes each reported figure was actually
# measured in. That is the same failure the 2026-09-12 rewrite fixed, one layer
# down. A wave's dot-prefixed sibling worlds stay tracked.
!/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/.*.omniworld

# ...but NOT `.harness_*`, which is the one dot-prefixed sibling the engine
# writes for itself rather than the one we author. `**/.harness_*.omniworld`
# near the top of this file says so everywhere else in the tree; the re-include
# above is a later rule, so inside a reply wave it undid that. Re-excluded here,
# after it, because last match wins. (13 are already tracked from the window
# when the re-include covered them; tracked files ignore .gitignore, so they
# stay put -- this only stops new ones joining them.)
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/.harness_*.omniworld
/social/launch/pilots/replies_*/**/.harness_*.wbt

# Third-party CAD submitted for an evaluation (2026-09-12): fusion_bot.urdf and
# 4.3 MB of STL wheels, dropped beside the chat worlds while evaluating a
# correspondent's robot. Not ours to vendor -- it needs a PROVENANCE.md and a
# licence answer first, and projects/ ships in the public snapshot.
/projects/samples/demos/worlds/chat/.eval912_rachit/

# Outreach send machinery working state: harvested contact pools, composed
# message bodies and per-round send batches. 16 MB and ~1,470 addresses, never
# tracked (0 commits), and not something to write into permanent history. The
# written records are tracked instead -- the ledger CSV, its reconstruction
# note, the operations handover and each wave's reports -- and they are what
# anyone actually needs.
# WARNING: ignored, not tracked, means `git clean -fdx` deletes all of it. Back
# it up outside the repo, where the suppression master already lives.
/social/launch/pipeline/
/social/launch/_send*.json
